  "meetings": {
   "meetings": {
    "__map": [
     [
      "MTG-1",
      {
       "id": "MTG-1",
       "kind": "meeting",
       "title": "Kickoff: Pip and the Night",
       "chair": "editor",
       "invitees": [
        "editor",
        "writer-1",
        "writer-2"
       ],
       "booking": "BK-1",
       "room": "story-room",
       "channel": "lane:e",
       "opened": 29876523.62005,
       "state": "open",
       "agenda": [
        {
         "n": 1,
         "title": "The arc: what happens on each of the five pages (Pip afraid → meets night friends → not afraid)",
         "item": null,
         "goal": "G-3",
         "rounds": [
          {
           "n": 1,
           "positions": {
            "writer-2": {
             "text": "P1: Bedtime in the den. Pip pulls his tail over his eyes; outside, the dark is big and full of sounds. P2: A crackle! Pip peeks out, shaking. A glow blinks by: a firefly, lost from her friends. P3: Pip forgets to be scared and follows her into the dark to help. P4: The sounds turn out to be friends: an owl hooting hello, crickets singing, a hedgehog snuffling. P5: Firefly home, Pip curls up outside under the stars, listening. \"Goodnight, night.\"",
             "t": 29876524.64435
            },
            "writer-1": {
             "text": "P1: Bedtime in the den. Shadows look huge; Pip pulls her tail over her eyes: The dark is too big. P2: A soft hoo-hoo. Pip peeks out the den door and meets Owl, who says wait and look; slowly the stars appear. P3: Fireflies blink a little path just outside the den, and Pip takes three brave steps. P4: The rustle is Hedgehog; the chirring is Cricket. Scary sounds now have names. P5: Back in bed, door open a crack, Pip says goodnight to each friend and sleeps.",
             "t": 29876524.746183332
            }
           },
           "revealed": false
          }
         ],
         "objections": [],
         "decision": null,
         "deferred": null
        },
        {
         "n": 2,
         "title": "Tone and the night friends: who they are, how they sound",
         "item": null,
         "goal": "G-3",
         "rounds": [
          {
           "n": 1,
           "positions": {
            "writer-2": {
             "text": "Tone: warm, hushed, a whisper-to-read-aloud book; short sentences, gentle repetition (\"Who is there?\"), soft sound words a 4-year-old can join in on. Friends, each turning a scary sound into a kind one: Glim the firefly (small, brave, chirpy, speaks in quick bright bits), Old Hoo the owl (slow, deep, kind: \"Hoo-hoo, hello\"), the cricket choir (a chorus, \"cree-cree\"), Bristle the hedgehog (shy, snuffly, like Pip). No villain; the dark itself is never punished or explained away.",
             "t": 29876524.6461
            },
            "writer-1": {
             "text": "Tone: hushed and warm, read-aloud rhythm, short lines, one refrain per page: What is that in the night? No villain, no real danger, and nobody tells Pip her fear is silly; friends show, they do not lecture. Friends: Owl (slow, low, kind; Hoo is there? Only me), Fireflies (tiny, giggly, rhyming: blink, wink, follow the light), Cricket (rhythmic sound words: chirr-chirr, sing-song), Hedgehog (shy and snuffly, scared of Pip at first, which mirrors her).",
             "t": 29876524.748316668
            }
           },
           "revealed": false
          }
         ],
         "objections": [],
         "decision": null,
         "deferred": null
        }
       ],
       "board": {
        "ideas": [
         {
          "by": "writer-2",
          "text": "Refrain on every page: \"Who is there?\" Pages 1-2 it is scared, pages 4-5 it is curious; the same words show the change.",
          "t": 29876524.6475
         },
         {
          "by": "writer-1",
          "text": "Keep Pip within sight of the den (and a grown-up fox) the whole time: ages 4-6 should not see wandering off alone at night modelled as brave. Bravery = peeking and a few steps, not a journey.",
          "t": 29876524.7501
         }
        ]
       },
       "present": {
